"ຖ້າລາຍງານນັ້ນຍັງຂາດຂໍ້ມູນບາງຢ່າງ, ທ່ານສາມາດເພີ່ມຂໍ້ມູນເຂົ້າໄປເພື່ອຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ນັກພັດທະນາແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ໄວຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:26
msgid "Reproduce the issue you've found"
msgstr "ລອງເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັນຫາຄືນໃໝ່"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:28
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Next, find out exactly how to recreate the bug that you've found. Document "
"the exact steps that you took to find the problem in detail. Then, reboot "
"your phone and perform those steps again. If the problem still occurs, "
"continue on to the next step. `If not... <https://youtu.be/nn2FB1P_Mn8?"
"t=10s>`_"
msgstr ""
"ລອງທົດສອບຂັ້ນຕອນທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດບັກຄືນໃໝ່ຫຼັງຈາກ reboot ເຄື່ອງ. ຖ້າບັນຫາຍັງເກີດຂຶ້ນຢູ່ "
"ໃຫ້ດຳເນີນການຂັ້ນຕໍ່ໄປ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:31
msgid "Making the bug report"
msgstr "ການສ້າງລາຍງານບັກ"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:33
msgid ""
"Now it's time for what you've been waiting for, the bug report itself! Bug "
"reports need to be filed in English."
msgstr "ລາຍງານບັກຈະຕ້ອງຂຽນເປັນພາສາອັງກິດ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:35
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First, pull up the `bug tracker <https://gitlab.com/ubports/development/"
"ubuntu-touch>`_ and click \"New Issue\". Log in to GitHub if you haven't yet."
msgstr "ເປີດ `bug tracker`_ ແລ້ວຄລິກ \"New Issue\" (ຕ້ອງເຂົ້າສູ່ລະບົບ GitHub ກ່ອນ)."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:37
msgid ""
"Next, you'll need to name your bug. Pick a name that says what's happening, "
"but don't be too wordy. Four to eight words should be enough."
msgstr "ຕັ້ງຊື່ບັກໃຫ້ເຂົ້າໃຈງ່າຍ ສັ້ນໆປະມານ 4-8 ຄຳ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:39
msgid "Now, write your bug report. A good bug report includes the following:"
msgstr "ລາຍງານບັກທີ່ດີຄວນປະກອບດ້ວຍສິ່ງຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:41
msgid "What happened: A synopsis of the erroneous behavior"
msgstr "ເກີດຫຍັງຂຶ້ນ: ສະຫຼຸບພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ຜິດພາດ"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:42
msgid ""
"What I expected to happen: A synopsis of what should have happened, if there "
"wasn't an error"
msgstr "ສິ່ງທີ່ຄາດຫວັງ: ສິ່ງທີ່ມັນຄວນຈະເປັນຖ້າບໍ່ມີຂໍ້ຜິດພາດ"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:43
msgid "Steps to reproduce: You wrote these down earlier, right?"
msgstr "ຂັ້ນຕອນການເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດຊ້ຳ: ທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ບັນທຶກໄວ້ກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:44
msgid ""
"Software Version: Go to (Settings - About) and list what appears on the "
"\"OS\" line of this screen. Also include the release channel that you used "
"when you installed Ubuntu on this phone."
msgstr ""
"ເວີຊັນຊອບແວ: ຂໍ້ມູນຈາກໜ້າ (ຕັ້ງຄ່າ - ກ່ຽວກັບ) ໃນແຖວ \"OS\" ແລະ ຊ່ອງທາງການຕິດຕັ້ງ (release "
"channel)."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:46
msgid ""
"Once you're finished with that, post the report. You can't add labels "
"yourself, so please don't forget to state the device you're experiencing the "
"issue on in the description so a moderator can easily add the correct tags "
"later."
msgstr "ເມື່ອຂຽນແລ້ວໃຫ້ໂພສລາຍງານ ແລະ ຢ່າລືມລະບຸຊື່ອຸປະກອນຂອງທ່ານນຳ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:48
msgid ""
"A developer or QA-team member will confirm and triage your bug, then work "
"can begin on it. If you are missing any information, you will be asked for "
"it, so make sure to check in often!"
msgstr ""
"ນັກພັດທະນາ ຫຼື ທີມ QA ຈະກວດສອບບັກຂອງທ່ານ. ຖ້າຂໍ້ມູນບໍ່ຄົບຖ້ວນ ພວກເຂົາອາດຈະຖາມຂໍ້ມູນເພີ່ມເຕີມ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:51
msgid "Getting Logs"
msgstr "ການເກັບ Logs"

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:53
msgid ""
"Here we'll discuss the general steps to get logs, files that contain "
"important debugging messages, on Ubuntu Touch. You may be asked for logs "
"after submitting your issue. This section will help you to retrieve these "
"logs from the device."
msgstr "logs ແມ່ນໄຟລ໌ທີ່ບັນທຶກຂໍ້ຄວາມການດີບັກທີ່ສຳຄັນ. ພາກນີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ທ່ານດຶງຂໍ້ມູນ logs ຈາກອຸປະກອນ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:57
msgid ""
"Log files may contain information you prefer to keep private. Please be sure "
"to skim through them to ensure this is not the case before posting them. We "
"can coordinate to get them through e-mail or a similarly less public medium."
msgstr "ໝາຍເຫດ: ໄຟລ໌ Log ອາດມີຂໍ້ມູນສ່ວນຕົວ. ກະລຸນາກວດສອບກ່ອນທີ່ຈະໂພສ."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:59
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"To get ready, download the `Logviewer app <https://open-store.io/app/"
"logviewer.ruditimmer>`_ from the OpenStore. This app will help us find, "
"view, and send the logs we need."
msgstr "ຕິດຕັ້ງແອັບ `Logviewer`_ ຈາກ OpenStore ເພື່ອຊ່ວຍໃນການເບິ່ງ ແລະ ສົ່ງ log."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:61
msgid ""
"Now, open the Logviewer app. You'll see the list of applications running on "
"your device. You can open any of them to view the logs of this application. "
"And you can use the \"send\" icon in the top right corner to share a log "
"using an online service."
msgstr "ໃນແອັບ Logviewer, ທ່ານສາມາດເລືອກເບິ່ງ log ຂອງແອັບຕ່າງໆ ແລະ ສົ່ງໃຫ້ທີມງານໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/bugreporting.rst:64
msgid ""
"If you don't see the log that you've been asked to send in Logviewer, it may "
"be in a different folder or the application may not have created any logs "
"yet. Tell this to the person who asked you for the logs. They should be able "
"to get you the information you need to get back on track."
msgstr "ຖ້າບໍ່ພົບ log ທີ່ຕ້ອງການ, ໃຫ້ແຈ້ງຜູ້ທີ່ຂໍ log ຈາກທ່ານ ເພື່ອຫາວິທີອື່ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:2
msgid "Code changes"
msgstr "ການປ່ຽນແປງໂຄ້ດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:4
msgid ""
"This page helps you get your changes to Ubuntu Touch merged. We describe the "
"things we look for in code, commits, and changesets. We also take a look at "
"what to expect in the code review process."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້ານີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ການປ່ຽນແປງໂຄ້ດຂອງທ່ານຖືກຮວມ (merge) ເຂົ້າສູ່ Ubuntu Touch. "
"ພວກເຮົາມີຂະບວນການກວດສອບໂຄ້ດເພື່ອຄວາມປອດໄພ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:7
msgid "Assumptions"
msgstr "ຂໍ້ຕົກລົງເບື້ອງຕົ້ນ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:9
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This page does not include information about how to develop applications or "
"changes to Ubuntu Touch. To learn how to develop Ubuntu Touch components, "
"see the :doc:`/systemdev/index` section. To learn how to develop "
"applications, see the :doc:`/appdev/index` or :doc:`/contribute/preinstalled-"
"apps` sections."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້ານີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນຄູ່ມືການພັດທະນາແອັບ. ຖ້າຕ້ອງການຮຽນຮູ້ການພັດທະນາໃຫ້ໄປເບິ່ງທີ່ພາກ :doc:`/systemdev/"
"index` ຫຼື :doc:`/appdev/index`."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:11
msgid ""
"This page assumes you know how to write your changes, use Git to commit "
"them, push them to GitHub or Gitlab as needed, fork a repository, and make a "
"Pull Request (PR) on GitHub or Merge Request (MR) on GitLab."
msgstr "ສົມມຸດວ່າທ່ານຮູ້ຈັກການໃຊ້ Git, ການ fork ແລະ ການສ້າງ Pull Request (PR) ຢູ່ແລ້ວ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:14
msgid "Definitions"
msgstr "ຄຳນິຍາມ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:16
msgid ""
"Since we use GitHub and GitLab for our code hosting depending on the "
"component, we use some terms interchangeably in this document."
msgstr "ເນື່ອງຈາກພວກເຮົານຳໃຊ້ທັງ GitHub ແລະ GitLab, ພວກເຮົາອາດຈະໃຊ້ບາງຄຳສັບແທນກັນໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:18
msgid "changeset"
msgstr "ຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງ (changeset)"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:19
msgid "A GitHub Pull Request (PR) or GitLab Merge Request (MR)."
msgstr "ໝາຍເຖິງ GitHub Pull Request (PR) ຫຼື GitLab Merge Request (MR)."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:20
msgid "issue report"
msgstr "ລາຍງານບັນຫາ (issue report)"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:21
msgid "A GitHub or GitLab Issue."
msgstr "ໝາຍເຖິງ Issue ໃນ GitHub ຫຼື GitLab."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:24
msgid "Reasoning"
msgstr "ເຫດຜົນ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:26
msgid ""
"Many users use Ubuntu Touch on many different devices. Breaking "
"functionality that these users rely on can be catastrophic. Our review "
"process helps us avoid broken functionality by ensuring a few properties of "
"the changeset."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ລະບົບມີບັນຫາອາດສົ່ງຜົນກະທົບຕໍ່ຜູ້ໃຊ້ຈຳນວນຫຼາຍ. "
"ຂະບວນການກວດສອບຂອງພວກເຮົາຈຶ່ງມີຄວາມສຳຄັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:28
msgid "In particular, we want to make sure the change:"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າການປ່ຽນແປງນັ້ນ:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:30
msgid "meets its own goals, such as adding a feature or fixing a bug"
msgstr "ບັນລຸເປົ້າໝາຍ ເຊັ່ນ: ເພີ່ມຟີເຈີ ຫຼື ແກ້ບັກໄດ້ແທ້"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:31
msgid "does not cause any unexpected behavior"
msgstr "ບໍ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ເກີດພຶດຕິກຳທີ່ບໍ່ຄາດຄິດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:32
msgid ""
"makes it easy for someone to make further changes to the software in the "
"future"
msgstr "ເຮັດໃຫ້ງ່າຍຕໍ່ການພັດທະນາຕໍ່ໃນອະນາຄົດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:35
msgid ""
"The rules on this page explain how you should write and document your "
"changes to Ubuntu Touch. Following these rules makes the review process "
"easier for you and us."
msgstr "ການປະຕິບັດຕາມກົດລະບຽບເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ຂະບວນການກວດສອບງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:37
msgid ""
"These are not absolute; we won't automatically reject your change based on "
"whether you follow the rules. If you break a rule, make sure you can explain "
"why."
msgstr "ກົດລະບຽບເຫຼົ່ານີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນຂໍ້ບັງຄັບຕາຍຕົວ, ແຕ່ຖ້າທ່ານບໍ່ປະຕິບັດຕາມ ທ່ານຕ້ອງມີເຫດຜົນທີ່ອະທິບາຍໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:40
msgid "Code change checklist"
msgstr "ລາຍການກວດສອບການປ່ຽນແປງໂຄ້ດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:42
msgid ""
"Keep this checklist in mind while writing your code and as you prepare to "
"commit your changes."
msgstr "ໃຫ້ກວດສອບຕາມລາຍການນີ້ກ່ອນທີ່ຈະສົ່ງມອບ (commit) ການປ່ຽນແປງ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:45
msgid "Do not commit commented code"
msgstr "ຢ່າ commit ໂຄ້ດທີ່ຖືກ comment ໄວ້"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:47
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"As developers, we often comment out code that is only there to help us "
"verify assumptions (like console logging messages). Make sure this **never** "
"makes it into your commits. If you must disobey this rule, make sure you add "
"a comment explaining why the commented code still exists in the source. If "
"you feel like you must make a ``// TODO:`` or ``// FIXME:`` comment, "
"consider whether filing an issue report referencing the broken code or TODO "
"item would be better."
msgstr ""
"ກວດສອບໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າບໍ່ມີໂຄ້ດທີ່ຖືກ comment ໄວ້ (ເຊັ່ນ console log) ຫຼຸດເຂົ້າໄປໃນ commit. "
"ຖ້າຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງມີ ໃຫ້ອະທິບາຍເຫດຜົນໄວ້ນຳ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:50
msgid "Write tests for your changes"
msgstr "ຂຽນການທົດສອບສຳລັບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:52
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"If a component has a test suite, use it. Make sure that you know how to run "
"the tests for the component and understand the output of those tests. The "
"component's README file should contain this information. If not and you "
"don't know how to find it, ask us. We're happy to help when someone is "
"trying to learn about a component for the first time. However, be prepared "
"to get a pile of links to documentation for a build system or test framework "
"rather than a hand-crafted list of commands for you to run. That may be all "
"we have time to provide. If you're still confused after checking out the "
"materials you've received, feel free to ask again with your new, specific "
"concerns. We would **really** appreciate it if you added your newfound "
"knowledge to the component's README. The best time to write documentation is "
"after doing something for the first time."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າສ່ວນປະກອບນັ້ນມີຊຸດການທົດສອບ (test suite) ໃຫ້ໃຊ້ມັນສະເໝີ. ທ່ານສາມາດເບິ່ງວິທີໃຊ້ໄດ້ຈາກໄຟລ໌ "
"README."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:54
msgid ""
"Once you know how to run the test suite, you can add your tests. Make sure "
"you test as many aspects of your new functionality as you feel are "
"reasonable. Lean on the side of more tests: we rarely ask you to remove "
"tests, but we may ask you to add more."
msgstr "ໃຫ້ຂຽນການທົດສອບໃຫ້ຄອບຄຸມຟີເຈີໃໝ່ທີ່ທ່ານເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໄປ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:56
msgid ""
"If you notice that a component doesn't have a test suite, it's an excellent "
"time to file a bug on that component! We would appreciate your help adding a "
"test suite, but we do not require that of you."
msgstr "ຖ້າພົບວ່າສ່ວນປະກອບໃດບໍ່ມີຊຸດການທົດສອບ, ທ່ານສາມາດແຈ້ງບັກ ຫຼື ຊ່ວຍເພີ່ມມັນເຂົ້າໄປໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:59
msgid "Follow any existing style guides"
msgstr "ປະຕິບັດຕາມຄູ່ມືຮູບແບບທີ່ມີຢູ່"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:61
msgid ""
"If a repository has a style guide, use it. If there is no style guide, try "
"to follow the existing style in the file you're changing as closely as "
"possible."
msgstr "ຖ້າມີຄູ່ມືຮູບແບບ (style guide) ໃຫ້ປະຕິບັດຕາມ. ຖ້າບໍ່ມີ ໃຫ້ຂຽນຕາມຮູບແບບເດີມຂອງໄຟລ໌ນັ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:64
msgid "Commit checklist"
msgstr "ລາຍການກວດສອບການຄອມມິດ (Commit checklist)"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:66
msgid ""
"Long after writing code, we often need to understand how and why it "
"introduces a bug. Commit messages are our first step in understanding these "
"complex questions. This checklist helps future viewers of your code "
"understand why it is the way it is."
msgstr ""
"ຂໍ້ຄວາມຄອມມິດ (Commit message) "
"ແມ່ນສິ່ງສຳຄັນທີ່ຈະຊ່ວຍໃຫ້ຄົນອື່ນເຂົ້າໃຈວ່າເປັນຫຍັງທ່ານຈຶ່ງປ່ຽນແປງໂຄ້ດແບບນັ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:68
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"For an example of a series of commits that follows these guidelines very "
"well, see the three commits at the top of the `git log leading to 840777f in "
"Lomiri <https://github.com/ubports/unity8/commits/"
"840777f92fb663a525dbe765155dbcf2a6f7541e>`_. Not every change requires such "
"an in-depth description as these examples. Lean on the side of more detail; "
"someday, *you* are the one looking back at your commits and wondering why "
"you made them."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ຂຽນລາຍລະອຽດໃຫ້ຊັດເຈນ ເພາະໃນອະນາຄົດທ່ານເອງອາດຈະກັບມາເບິ່ງແລ້ວສົງໄສວ່າເປັນຫຍັງຈຶ່ງເຮັດແບບນັ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:71
msgid "Answer crucial questions in commit messages"
msgstr "ຕອບຄຳຖາມທີ່ສຳຄັນໃນຂໍ້ຄວາມຄອມມິດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:73
msgid ""
"We ask questions like, \"what?\" \"why?\" and \"how?\" to gain context of a "
"situation quickly."
msgstr ""
"ໃຫ້ຕອບຄຳຖາມວ່າ \"ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?\", \"ເປັນຫຍັງ?\" ແລະ \"ແນວໃດ?\" ເພື່ອໃຫ້ຄົນອື່ນເຂົ້າໃຈບໍລິບົດໄດ້ໄວ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:75
msgid ""
"Strive to answer these questions in your commit metadata or content. Doing "
"so helps reviewers and future readers understand the context of a change. In "
"order of importance, answer:"
msgstr "ພະຍາຍາມຕອບຄຳຖາມເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນ metadata ຫຼື ເນື້ອຫາຂອງການຄອມມິດ ຕາມລຳດັບຄວາມສຳຄັນດັ່ງນີ້:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:77
msgid "What?"
msgstr "ແມ່ນຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:78
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Answer this question with the first few lines of your commit message. \"What "
"does your commit do?\" \"`Optimize wallpapers for load times and memory use "
"<https://github.com/ubports/unity8/commit/"
"a81421ac1fe5135b9cff710c3cd819aa1804c6e6>`_\"."
msgstr ""
"ຕອບໃນສອງສາມແຖວທຳອິດວ່າການຄອມມິດນີ້ເຮັດຫຍັງ. ເຊັ່ນ: \"ປັບປຸງພາບພື້ນຫຼັງໃຫ້ໂຫຼດໄວຂຶ້ນ ແລະ "
"ປະຢັດຄວາມຈຳ\"."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:79
msgid "Why?"
msgstr "ເປັນຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:80
msgid ""
"Always state the reasoning behind a change: the bugs it fixes, the features "
"it builds up to, and especially the limitations that cause it to look more "
"complicated than a viewer expects. Provide permanent links to issue reports "
"or documentation if they give context."
msgstr "ບອກເຫດຜົນເບື້ອງຫຼັງການປ່ຽນແປງສະເໝີ ເຊັ່ນ: ແກ້ບັກໃດ, ເພີ່ມຟີເຈີຫຍັງ ແລະ ໃຫ້ລິ້ງອ້າງອີງຖ້າມີ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:81
msgid "Who?"
msgstr "ໃຜ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:82
msgid ""
"Git embeds your name and email address as the committer of your changes. If "
"someone else has helped you write your changes, you should add them with a "
"``Co-Authored-By: Their Name <their-email@example.com>`` line in your commit "
"message."
msgstr ""
"Git ຝັງຊື່ ແລະ ທີ່ຢູ່ອີເມວຂອງທ່ານໃນຖານະຜູ້ commit (committer) ການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ. "
"ຖ້າຄົນອື່ນໄດ້ຊ່ວຍທ່ານຂຽນການປ່ຽນແປງ, ທ່ານຄວນເພີ່ມພວກເຂົາດ້ວຍແຖວ ``Co-Authored-By: "
"ຊື່ຂອງພວກເຂົາ <their-email@example.com>`` ໃນຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit ຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:84
msgid ""
"It is possible to provide some of this context in code comments rather than "
"in commit messages. Comments can assist people who are only reading the code "
"without using tools like ``git blame``. Bear in mind that comments can "
"quickly become out-of-date compared to the code that they are near. A commit "
"message is linked only to the code you wrote."
msgstr ""
"ມັນເປັນໄປໄດ້ທີ່ຈະໃຫ້ບໍລິບົດບາງຢ່າງເຫຼົ່ານີ້ໃນຄຳເຫັນຂອງໂຄດ ແທນທີ່ຈະຢູ່ໃນຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit. "
"ຄຳເຫັນສາມາດຊ່ວຍຄົນທີ່ອ່ານພຽງແຕ່ໂຄດໂດຍບໍ່ຕ້ອງໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືເຊັ່ນ ``git blame``. ຈົ່ງຈື່ໄວ້ວ່າ "
"ຄຳເຫັນສາມາດລ້າສະໄໝໄດ້ໄວເມື່ອທຽບກັບໂຄດທີ່ພວກມັນຢູ່ໃກ້. ຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit "
"ແມ່ນເຊື່ອມໂຍງກັບໂຄດທີ່ທ່ານຂຽນເທົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:86
msgid ""
"In closing, make sure you anticipate any questions you expect yourself or "
"others to have about your code in the future and answer them."
msgstr ""
"ສະຫຼຸບແລ້ວ, ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າທ່ານໄດ້ຄາດການຄຳຖາມໃດໆທີ່ທ່ານເອງ ຫຼື "
"ຄົນອື່ນອາດຈະມີກ່ຽວກັບໂຄດຂອງທ່ານໃນອະນາຄົດ ແລະ ຕອບຄຳຖາມເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:89
msgid "Make commits as small as possible, but no smaller"
msgstr "ເຮັດໃຫ້ commits ນ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້, ແຕ່ບໍ່ໃຫ້ມັນນ້ອຍເກີນໄປ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:91
msgid ""
"Some changes require multiple logical steps to complete. If this is the "
"case, split these steps into separate commits. Each commit should follow the "
"entire commit checklist. It should not require any of the commits that come "
"after it to build or pass tests."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນແປງບາງຢ່າງຮຽກຮ້ອງໃຫ້ມີຫຼາຍຂັ້ນຕອນຕາມລຳດັບເຫດຜົນເພື່ອໃຫ້ສຳເລັດ. ຖ້າເປັນກໍລະນີນີ້, "
"ໃຫ້ແບ່ງຂັ້ນຕອນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ອອກເປັນ commits ແຍກກັນ. ແຕ່ລະ commit ຄວນປະຕິບັດຕາມລາຍການກວດສອບ "
"commit ທັງໝົດ. ມັນບໍ່ຄວນຕ້ອງການ commit ໃດໆທີ່ມາຫຼັງຈາກມັນເພື່ອ build ຫຼື ຜ່ານການທົດສອບ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:93
msgid ""
"Let's say you are implementing a new way to search for phone numbers in the "
"Dialer app. Your change requires three distinct steps:"
msgstr ""
"ສົມມຸດວ່າທ່ານກຳລັງພັດທະນາວິທີການໃໝ່ໃນການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບໃນແອັບຯ Dialer. "
"ການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານຕ້ອງການສາມຂັ້ນຕອນທີ່ແຕກຕ່າງກັນ:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:95
msgid "Fix a bug in the current phone number search"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂບັກ (bug) ໃນການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບປັດຈຸບັນ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:96
msgid "Add a new API to support your new number search"
msgstr "ເພີ່ມ API ໃໝ່ເພື່ອຮອງຮັບການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບໃໝ່ຂອງທ່ານ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:97
msgid "Add the UI elements to use your new search"
msgstr "ເພີ່ມອົງປະກອບ UI ເພື່ອໃຊ້ການຄົ້ນຫາໃໝ່ຂອງທ່ານ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:99
msgid ""
"If you do all of these changes in a single commit and there is a problem in "
"step three, we reject the entire changeset. If you split the changes into "
"separate commits instead, the bug fix and new API could be added to the "
"mainline software while you work on redesigning your UI."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານເຮັດການປ່ຽນແປງທັງໝົດນີ້ໃນ commit ດຽວ ແລະ ມີບັນຫາໃນຂັ້ນຕອນທີສາມ, "
"ພວກເຮົາຈະປະຕິເສດຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງ (changeset) ທັງໝົດ. ຖ້າທ່ານແບ່ງການປ່ຽນແປງອອກເປັນ commits "
"ແຍກກັນ, ການແກ້ໄຂບັກ ແລະ API ໃໝ່ສາມາດຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນຊອບແວຫຼັກ (mainline) "
"ໃນຂະນະທີ່ທ່ານຍັງເຮັດວຽກອອກແບບ UI ຂອງທ່ານໃໝ່."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:102
msgid "Rebase your changes during the review, if possible"
msgstr "Rebase ການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານໃນລະຫວ່າງການກວດສອບ, ຖ້າເປັນໄປໄດ້"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:104
msgid "It's common for a commit log on GitHub to go something like this:"
msgstr "ມັນເປັນເລື່ອງປົກກະຕິສຳລັບບັນທຶກ commit (commit log) ໃນ GitHub ທີ່ຈະເປັນແບບນີ້:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:106
msgid "Fix bug in phone number search"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂບັກໃນການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:107
msgid "Add new API call for new phone number search"
msgstr "ເພີ່ມການຮ້ອງຂໍ API ໃໝ່ສຳລັບການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບໃໝ່"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:108
msgid "Add UI for new phone number search"
msgstr "ເພີ່ມ UI ສຳລັບການຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບໃໝ່"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:109
msgid "Fix UI"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂ UI"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:110
msgid "Fix bug fix"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂການແກ້ໄຂບັກ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:111
msgid "Review changes"
msgstr "ກວດສອບການປ່ຽນແປງ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:112
msgid "Fix API after comments from reviewers"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂ API ຫຼັງຈາກໄດ້ຮັບຄຳເຫັນຈາກຜູ້ກວດສອບ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:114
msgid ""
"If you have to come back to this commit log in the future, you'll be "
"confused in no time at all. What did the reviewers say, what was wrong with "
"the UI and the bug fix?"
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງໄດ້ກັບມາເບິ່ງບັນທຶກ commit ນີ້ໃນອະນາຄົດ, ທ່ານຈະສັບສົນໃນທັນທີ. ຜູ້ກວດສອບເວົ້າຫຍັງ, "
"ມີຫຍັງຜິດພາດກັບ UI ແລະ ການແກ້ໄຂບັກ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:116
msgid ""
"Don't add a new commit when you receive a correction that affects the first "
"commit in your series. Instead, edit the first commit. If doing this changes "
"the information in your commit message, update that too."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າເພີ່ມ commit ໃໝ່ເມື່ອທ່ານໄດ້ຮັບຄຳແນະນຳໃຫ້ແກ້ໄຂທີ່ມີຜົນຕໍ່ commit ທຳອິດໃນຊຸດຂອງທ່ານ. "
"ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນແນວນັ້ນ, ໃຫ້ແກ້ໄຂທີ່ commit ທຳອິດນັ້ນເລີຍ. ຖ້າການເຮັດແບບນີ້ປ່ຽນແປງຂໍ້ມູນໃນຂໍ້ຄວາມ "
"commit ຂອງທ່ານ, ໃຫ້ອັບເດດມັນເຊັ່ນກັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:118
msgid ""
"Editing commits requires learning new tools in Git. Edit a series of commits "
"with ``git-rebase``. Push the resulting changes with a force push, or create "
"a new branch and open a new changeset."
msgstr ""
"ການແກ້ໄຂ commits ຮຽກຮ້ອງໃຫ້ຮຽນຮູ້ເຄື່ອງມືໃໝ່ໃນ Git. ແກ້ໄຂຊຸດຂອງ commits ດ້ວຍ ``git-"
"rebase``. ສົ່ງ (Push) ການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ໄດ້ຮັບດ້ວຍ force push, ຫຼື ສ້າງ branch ໃໝ່ ແລະ "
"ເປີດຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງໃໝ່."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:120
msgid ""
"Luckily, there are graphical tools that make this job more manageable. "
"Unluckily, if you don't understand what they are doing on the Git command "
"line, you might mess up and have to start over from your old series. Even "
"seasoned Git pros mess up this process sometimes, don't worry. There is "
"almost always a way back to your old series."
msgstr ""
"ໂຊກດີ, ມີເຄື່ອງມືກຣາຟິກທີ່ເຮັດໃຫ້ວຽກງານນີ້ຈັດການໄດ້ງ່າຍຂຶ້ນ. ແຕ່ໂຊກຮ້າຍ, "
"ຖ້າທ່ານບໍ່ເຂົ້າໃຈສິ່ງທີ່ພວກເຂົາກຳລັງເຮັດຢູ່ໃນ Git command line, ທ່ານອາດຈະເຮັດໃຫ້ມັນຫຍຸ້ງ ແລະ "
"ຕ້ອງເລີ່ມຕົ້ນໃໝ່ຈາກຊຸດເກົ່າຂອງທ່ານ. ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າຜູ້ຊ່ຽວຊານ Git ກໍຍັງເຮັດຜິດພາດໃນຂະບວນການນີ້ບາງຄັ້ງ, "
"ບໍ່ຕ້ອງກັງວົນ. ມັນເກືອບຈະມີວິທີກັບຄືນໄປຫາຊຸດເກົ່າຂອງທ່ານສະເໝີ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:122
msgid ""
"Each commit must continue to build, run, and pass tests after your changes."
msgstr ""
"ແຕ່ລະ commit ຕ້ອງສາມາດ build, ແລ່ນ, ແລະ ຜ່ານການທົດສອບໄດ້ຫຼັງຈາກການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:125
msgid "Format your commit message correctly"
msgstr "ຈັດຮູບແບບຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit ຂອງທ່ານໃຫ້ຖືກຕ້ອງ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:127
msgid ""
"Keep the first line of your commit message (the summary) to 50 characters or "
"less. Every other line in the commit message should be 72 characters or "
"less. It's OK if you have to break the rules — some changes can't be "
"summarized in 50 characters, and some links are longer than 72."
msgstr ""
"ຮັກສາແຖວທຳອິດຂອງຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit ຂອງທ່ານ (ບົດສະຫຼຸບ) ໃຫ້ຢູ່ໃນ 50 ຕົວອັກສອນ ຫຼື ໜ້ອຍກວ່າ. "
"ທຸກໆແຖວອື່ນໃນຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit ຄວນຈະເປັນ 72 ຕົວອັກສອນ ຫຼື ໜ້ອຍກວ່າ. "
"ມັນບໍ່ເປັນຫຍັງຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງຝ່າຝືນກົດລະບຽບ — ເພາະການປ່ຽນແປງບາງຢ່າງບໍ່ສາມາດສະຫຼຸບໄດ້ໃນ 50 ຕົວອັກສອນ, "
"ແລະ ລິ້ງບາງອັນກໍຍາວກວ່າ 72 ຕົວອັກສອນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:130
msgid "Changeset description checklist"
msgstr "ລາຍການກວດສອບຄຳອະທິບາຍຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:132
msgid ""
"Ensure that your changeset answers the following questions in its "
"description."
msgstr "ໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານໄດ້ຕອບຄຳຖາມຕໍ່ໄປນີ້ໃນຄຳອະທິບາຍຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:134
msgid ""
"If you've followed the guidelines for commit messages, you can probably copy "
"the relevant information from the commit messages into your changeset "
"description. GitHub and GitLab do this for you in single-commit changesets. "
"A description that says, \"this is complicated to explain; please read the "
"commit messages,\" is also acceptable. We trust you to strike a balance."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານໄດ້ປະຕິບັດຕາມຄຳແນະນຳສຳລັບຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit, ທ່ານອາດຈະສາມາດຄັດລອກຂໍ້ມູນທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງຈາກຂໍ້ຄວາມ "
"commit ເຂົ້າໄປໃນຄຳອະທິບາຍຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ. GitHub ແລະ GitLab "
"ເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໃຫ້ທ່ານສຳລັບຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ມີ commit ດຽວ. ຄຳອະທິບາຍທີ່ບອກວ່າ, \"ອັນນີ້ສັບສົນທີ່ຈະອະທິບາຍ; "
"ກະລຸນາອ່ານຂໍ້ຄວາມ commit,\" ກໍເປັນທີ່ຍອມຮັບໄດ້ເຊັ່ນກັນ. "
"ພວກເຮົາເຊື່ອໝັ້ນວ່າທ່ານຈະສາມາດຊອກຫາຄວາມສົມດຸນໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:137
msgid "What issue does your changeset resolve?"
msgstr "ຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາຫຍັງ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:139
msgid ""
"Link changesets to the issue report that they resolve, whether you add a "
"feature or fix a problem. Specify the devices the issue occurs on or if it "
"applies to all devices. Provide enough information so that someone can look "
"at it and know how to reproduce the problem or test the feature. Add this "
"information to the issue report as well if it is missing."
msgstr ""
"ເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງກັບບົດລາຍງານບັນຫາທີ່ພວກມັນແກ້ໄຂ, ບໍ່ວ່າທ່ານຈະເພີ່ມຄຸນສົມບັດ ຫຼື ແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາ. "
"ລະບຸອຸປະກອນທີ່ບັນຫາເກີດຂຶ້ນ ຫຼື ຖ້າມັນໃຊ້ກັບທຸກອຸປະກອນ. ໃຫ້ຂໍ້ມູນພຽງພໍເພື່ອໃຫ້ຄົນອື່ນສາມາດເບິ່ງມັນ ແລະ "
"ຮູ້ວິທີການເຮັດໃຫ້ບັນຫາເກີດຂຶ້ນຊ້ຳ ຫຼື ທົດສອບຄຸນສົມບັດ. ເພີ່ມຂໍ້ມູນນີ້ໃສ່ໃນບົດລາຍງານບັນຫາເຊັ່ນກັນ "
"ຖ້າມັນຂາດຫາຍໄປ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:141 ../../contribute/code.rst:150
msgid "For example:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງ:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:143
msgid "Fixes https://gitlab.com/ubports/development/ubuntu-touch/-/issues/1"
msgstr "ແກ້ໄຂ https://gitlab.com/ubports/development/ubuntu-touch/-/issues/1"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:146
msgid "How did you test that the change was successful?"
msgstr "ທ່ານໄດ້ທົດສອບແນວໃດວ່າການປ່ຽນແປງນັ້ນປະສົບຜົນສຳເລັດ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:148
msgid ""
"All changes require testing to ensure they resolve the issue report they're "
"referencing. List the environment you tested your changes in, including the "
"operating system under test, its version, and the devices you tested on. "
"Explain your testing process. If you are not sure how to test a feature "
"related to your changes, mention it."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນແປງທັງໝົດຕ້ອງການການທົດສອບເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າພວກມັນແກ້ໄຂບົດລາຍງານບັນຫາທີ່ພວກມັນອ້າງອີງ. "
"ລະບຸສະພາບແວດລ້ອມທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ທົດສອບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ, ລວມທັງລະບົບປະຕິບັດການທີ່ທົດສອບ, ລຸ້ນຂອງມັນ, "
"ແລະ ອຸປະກອນທີ່ທ່ານທົດສອບ. ອະທິບາຍຂະບວນການທົດສອບຂອງທ່ານ. "
"ຖ້າທ່ານບໍ່ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຈະທົດສອບຄຸນສົມບັດທີ່ກ່ຽວຂ້ອງກັບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານແນວໃດ, ໃຫ້ກ່າວເຖິງມັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:152
msgid ""
"I've tested this dialer change on the Nexus 5. It should work on all devices "
"since it's not modifying anything device-specific, but more testing would be "
"appreciated. To fix a bug, I had to touch a bit of code in the phone number "
"search area (#53). I'm not entirely sure how to test that for regressions."
msgstr ""
"ຂ້ອຍໄດ້ທົດສອບການປ່ຽນແປງ dialer ນີ້ໃນ Nexus 5. ມັນຄວນຈະເຮັດວຽກໃນທຸກອຸປະກອນ "
"ເນື່ອງຈາກມັນບໍ່ໄດ້ດັດແກ້ສິ່ງທີ່ສະເພາະເຈາະຈົງກັບອຸປະກອນ, ແຕ່ການທົດສອບເພີ່ມເຕີມຈະໄດ້ຮັບການຂອບໃຈ. "
"ເພື່ອແກ້ໄຂບັກ, ຂ້ອຍຕ້ອງແຕະຕ້ອງໂຄດເລັກນ້ອຍໃນພື້ນທີ່ຄົ້ນຫາເບີໂທລະສັບ (#53). "
"ຂ້ອຍບໍ່ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຈະທົດສອບສິ່ງນັ້ນສຳລັບ regressions ແນວໃດ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:155
msgid "Do any changes need to be merged before or after this changeset?"
msgstr "ມີການປ່ຽນແປງໃດໆທີ່ຕ້ອງໄດ້ຮັບການລວມເຂົ້າ (merged) ກ່ອນ ຫຼື ຫຼັງຈາກຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງນີ້ບໍ່?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:157
msgid ""
"Some changes depend on one or more changes before they work correctly. If "
"this is the case, you should document the dependencies in your changeset "
"descriptions. Document all sets that must be merged *before* and *after* the "
"current one in a series, if needed."
msgstr ""
"ການປ່ຽນແປງບາງຢ່າງຂຶ້ນກັບການປ່ຽນແປງໜຶ່ງ ຫຼື ຫຼາຍກວ່ານັ້ນກ່ອນທີ່ພວກມັນຈະເຮັດວຽກຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງ. "
"ຖ້າເປັນກໍລະນີນີ້, ທ່ານຄວນບັນທຶກການຂຶ້ນກັບກັນ (dependencies) ໃນຄຳອະທິບາຍຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ. "
"ບັນທຶກຊຸດທັງໝົດທີ່ຕ້ອງຖືກລວມເຂົ້າ *ກ່ອນ* ແລະ *ຫຼັງ* ຊຸດປັດຈຸບັນໃນຊຸດ, ຖ້າຈຳເປັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:159
msgid ""
"For example, say you've filed three Merge Requests on GitLab, ``ubports/core/"
"docs!1``, ``ubports/core/code!2``, and ``ubports/core/infrastructure!3``. "
"They must be merged in that order. In that case, your MR descriptions would "
"have something similar to this included:"
msgstr ""
"ຕົວຢ່າງ, ສົມມຸດວ່າທ່ານໄດ້ສົ່ງສາມ Merge Requests ໃນ GitLab, ``ubports/core/docs!1``, "
"``ubports/core/code!2``, ແລະ ``ubports/core/infrastructure!3``. "
"ພວກມັນຕ້ອງຖືກລວມເຂົ້າຕາມລຳດັບນັ້ນ. ໃນກໍລະນີນັ້ນ, ຄຳອະທິບາຍ MR "
"ຂອງທ່ານຈະມີບາງຢ່າງທີ່ຄ້າຍຄືກັນກັບສິ່ງນີ້ລວມຢູ່:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:161
msgid "In ``ubports/core/docs!1``:"
msgstr "ໃນ ``ubports/core/docs!1``:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:163
msgid ""
"ubports/core/code!2 and ubports/core/infrastructure!3 depend on this MR."
msgstr "ubports/core/code!2 ແລະ ubports/core/infrastructure!3 ຂຶ້ນກັບ MR ນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:164
msgid "In ``ubports/core/code!2``:"
msgstr "ໃນ ``ubports/core/code!2``:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:166
msgid ""
"ubports/docs!1 must be merged before this MR. ubports/core/infrastructure!3 "
"depends on this MR."
msgstr ""
"ubports/docs!1 ຕ້ອງຖືກລວມເຂົ້າກ່ອນ MR ນີ້. ubports/core/infrastructure!3 ຂຶ້ນກັບ MR ນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:167
msgid "In ``ubports/core/infrastructure!3``:"
msgstr "ໃນ ``ubports/core/infrastructure!3``:"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:169
msgid ""
"ubports/docs!1 and ubports/core/infrastructure!3 must be merged before this "
"MR."
msgstr "ubports/docs!1 ແລະ ubports/core/infrastructure!3 ຕ້ອງຖືກລວມເຂົ້າກ່ອນ MR ນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:172
msgid "What does the interface look like before and after the change?"
msgstr "ສ່ວນຕິດຕໍ່ຜູ້ໃຊ້ (interface) ເບິ່ງຄືແນວໃດກ່ອນ ແລະ ຫຼັງການປ່ຽນແປງ?"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:174
msgid ""
"If your changes also change the look of the user interface, include "
"screenshots to illustrate these changes."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານຍັງປ່ຽນຮູບລັກສະນະຂອງສ່ວນຕິດຕໍ່ຜູ້ໃຊ້, "
"ໃຫ້ລວມເອົາພາບໜ້າຈໍເພື່ອສະແດງການປ່ຽນແປງເຫຼົ່ານີ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:177
msgid "Submission and review"
msgstr "ການສົ່ງ ແລະ ການກວດສອບ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:179
msgid ""
"Now that you've checked your changeset, it's time to submit it for the "
"review! Thank you in advance for contributing to Ubuntu Touch. Here is what "
"you can expect from us as we review your changes."
msgstr ""
"ຕອນນີ້ທ່ານໄດ້ກວດສອບຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານແລ້ວ, ມັນເຖິງເວລາທີ່ຈະສົ່ງມັນເພື່ອການກວດສອບ! "
"ຂໍຂອບໃຈລ່ວງຫນ້າສຳລັບການປະກອບສ່ວນເຂົ້າໃນ Ubuntu Touch. "
"ນີ້ແມ່ນສິ່ງທີ່ທ່ານສາມາດຄາດຫວັງຈາກພວກເຮົາໃນຂະນະທີ່ພວກເຮົາກວດສອບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:182
msgid "We respect you"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາເຄົາລົບທ່ານ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:184
msgid ""
"You chose to use your time to contribute to Ubuntu Touch. That decision is "
"never made lightly. A reviewer must treat you with respect and work with you "
"toward your changeset becoming a part of Ubuntu Touch."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານເລືອກທີ່ຈະໃຊ້ເວລາຂອງທ່ານເພື່ອປະກອບສ່ວນເຂົ້າໃນ Ubuntu Touch. "
"ການຕັດສິນໃຈນັ້ນບໍ່ໄດ້ເຮັດແບບຫຼິ້ນໆ. ຜູ້ກວດສອບຕ້ອງປະຕິບັດຕໍ່ທ່ານດ້ວຍຄວາມເຄົາລົບ ແລະ "
"ເຮັດວຽກກັບທ່ານເພື່ອໃຫ້ຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານກາຍເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງ Ubuntu Touch."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:186
msgid ""
"Respect is a two-way street. Ubuntu Touch is a large project; there are "
"never enough hands to do all the work needed. It may take a while for your "
"changeset to see any attention, and after a long wait, you might come back "
"to find a stern request for changes. Read a stern-looking message as someone "
"trying to work as quickly as possible, not as an attempt to be rude to you. "
"We extend the same grace to you."
msgstr ""
"ຄວາມເຄົາລົບແມ່ນຖະໜົນສອງທາງ. Ubuntu Touch ແມ່ນໂຄງການຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່; "
"ບໍ່ເຄີຍມີມືພຽງພໍທີ່ຈະເຮັດວຽກທັງໝົດທີ່ຕ້ອງການ. "
"ມັນອາດຈະໃຊ້ເວລາໄລຍະໜຶ່ງສຳລັບຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານທີ່ຈະໄດ້ຮັບຄວາມສົນໃຈ, ແລະ ຫຼັງຈາກລໍຖ້າດົນນານ, "
"ທ່ານອາດຈະກັບມາພົບກັບຄຳຮ້ອງຂໍການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ເຂັ້ມງວດ. "
"ໃຫ້ອ່ານຂໍ້ຄວາມທີ່ເບິ່ງຄືວ່າເຂັ້ມງວດນັ້ນວ່າເປັນຄົນທີ່ພະຍາຍາມເຮັດວຽກໃຫ້ໄວທີ່ສຸດເທົ່າທີ່ຈະເປັນໄປໄດ້, "
"ບໍ່ແມ່ນຄວາມພະຍາຍາມທີ່ຈະຫຍາບຄາຍຕໍ່ທ່ານ. ພວກເຮົາສົ່ງຄວາມປາດຖະໜາດີດຽວກັນໃຫ້ທ່ານ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:189
msgid "We ask many questions"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາຖາມຫຼາຍຄຳຖາມ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:191
msgid ""
"Reviewers better understand the code you're changing after asking you "
"questions about how it works. They may know what your code does already, but "
"they'll still ask. If you can explain how your code works, it's more likely "
"that you have done the proper testing to ensure it works."
msgstr ""
"ຜູ້ກວດສອບເຂົ້າໃຈໂຄດທີ່ທ່ານກຳລັງປ່ຽນແປງໄດ້ດີຂຶ້ນຫຼັງຈາກຖາມທ່ານກ່ຽວກັບວິທີການເຮັດວຽກຂອງມັນ. "
"ພວກເຂົາອາດຈະຮູ້ວ່າໂຄດຂອງທ່ານເຮັດຫຍັງຢູ່ແລ້ວ, ແຕ່ພວກເຂົາຍັງຈະຖາມ. "
"ຖ້າທ່ານສາມາດອະທິບາຍວິທີການເຮັດວຽກຂອງໂຄດຂອງທ່ານ, "
"ມັນເປັນໄປໄດ້ຫຼາຍທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ເຮັດການທົດສອບທີ່ເໝາະສົມເພື່ອໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າມັນເຮັດວຽກ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:193
msgid ""
"If you are not able to articulate why something works, it is a red flag. The "
"change is likely working around a different bug that can come back to haunt "
"us in the future. Fixing the real bug instead of making workarounds is a "
"better use of time."
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານບໍ່ສາມາດອະທິບາຍໄດ້ວ່າເປັນຫຍັງບາງສິ່ງບາງຢ່າງຈຶ່ງເຮັດວຽກ, ມັນເປັນສັນຍານເຕືອນ. "
"ການປ່ຽນແປງນັ້ນອາດຈະເປັນການແກ້ໄຂແບບຊົ່ວຄາວສຳລັບບັກອື່ນທີ່ສາມາດກັບມາລົບກວນພວກເຮົາໃນອະນາຄົດ. "
"ການແກ້ໄຂບັກທີ່ແທ້ຈິງແທນທີ່ຈະເຮັດວິທີແກ້ໄຂຊົ່ວຄາວແມ່ນການໃຊ້ເວລາທີ່ດີກວ່າ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:196
msgid "We ask for changes"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາຮ້ອງຂໍການປ່ຽນແປງ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:198
msgid ""
"Another person looking at your code may see problems with it that you have "
"missed. Whether those problems are inefficiencies, style issues, or new "
"bugs, they are more likely to be found by your reviewers than by you. Don't "
"worry if you get a book of requested changes back from your reviewer. Nobody "
"is perfect. Finding and fixing these potential issues leads to a faster and "
"more stable Ubuntu Touch. It is not an insult to your skills as a developer."
msgstr ""
"ຄົນອື່ນທີ່ເບິ່ງໂຄດຂອງທ່ານອາດຈະເຫັນບັນຫາກັບມັນທີ່ທ່ານພາດໄປ. ບໍ່ວ່າບັນຫາເຫຼົ່ານັ້ນຈະເປັນການຂາດປະສິດທິພາບ, "
"ບັນຫາຮູບແບບ, ຫຼື ບັກໃໝ່, ພວກມັນມີແນວໂນ້ມທີ່ຈະຖືກພົບເຫັນໂດຍຜູ້ກວດສອບຂອງທ່ານຫຼາຍກວ່າໂດຍທ່ານ. "
"ບໍ່ຕ້ອງກັງວົນຖ້າທ່ານໄດ້ຮັບບັນຊີລາຍຊື່ຂອງການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ຮ້ອງຂໍຄືນຈາກຜູ້ກວດສອບຂອງທ່ານ. ບໍ່ມີໃຜສົມບູນແບບ. "
"ການຊອກຫາ ແລະ ການແກ້ໄຂບັນຫາທີ່ອາດຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຈະນຳໄປສູ່ Ubuntu Touch ທີ່ໄວຂຶ້ນ ແລະ "
"ໝັ້ນຄົງກວ່າ. ມັນບໍ່ແມ່ນການດູຖູກທັກສະຂອງທ່ານໃນຖານະນັກພັດທະນາ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:201
msgid "We may ask for massive changes"
msgstr "ພວກເຮົາອາດຈະຮ້ອງຂໍການປ່ຽນແປງຂະໜາດໃຫຍ່"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:203
msgid ""
"Sometimes reviewers look at a change and realize that a much deeper issue "
"exists in the component. Sometimes you start out developing a feature with "
"the wrong assumptions in mind and end up with an unwieldy mess of spaghetti "
"code. Either way: this is not the correct path to the destination. Whatever "
"the reason, your reviewer points out the potential problems with your change "
"and constructively suggests a new direction for you to take."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງຜູ້ກວດສອບເບິ່ງການປ່ຽນແປງ ແລະ ຮັບຮູ້ວ່າມີບັນຫາທີ່ເລິກເຊິ່ງກວ່າຢູ່ໃນອົງປະກອບນັ້ນ. "
"ບາງຄັ້ງທ່ານເລີ່ມຕົ້ນພັດທະນາຄຸນສົມບັດດ້ວຍສົມມຸດຕິຖານທີ່ຜິດ ແລະ ຈົບລົງດ້ວຍໂຄດທີ່ຫຍຸ້ງຍາກ. ບໍ່ວ່າທາງໃດ: "
"ນີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນເສັ້ນທາງທີ່ຖືກຕ້ອງໄປສູ່ຈຸດໝາຍປາຍທາງ. ບໍ່ວ່າຈະດ້ວຍເຫດຜົນໃດກໍຕາມ, "
"ຜູ້ກວດສອບຂອງທ່ານຈະຊີ້ໃຫ້ເຫັນບັນຫາທີ່ອາດຈະເກີດຂຶ້ນກັບການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານ ແລະ "
"ແນະນຳທິດທາງໃໝ່ໃຫ້ທ່ານປະຕິບັດຢ່າງສ້າງສັນ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:206
msgid "You can tell us that we are wrong"
msgstr "ທ່ານສາມາດບອກພວກເຮົາວ່າພວກເຮົາຜິດ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:208
msgid ""
"You might be sure that an underlying bug is not easily fixable or that the "
"path you've taken is the best. You might not have enough time to do a fix "
"correctly as asked. If you think that our rejection of your changeset is "
"wrong for any reason, let us know. Reviewers try to work with you to reach a "
"solution that's best for our users."
msgstr ""
"ທ່ານອາດຈະແນ່ໃຈວ່າບັກພື້ນຖານບໍ່ສາມາດແກ້ໄຂໄດ້ງ່າຍ ຫຼື ວ່າເສັ້ນທາງທີ່ທ່ານເລືອກແມ່ນດີທີ່ສຸດ. "
"ທ່ານອາດຈະບໍ່ມີເວລາພຽງພໍທີ່ຈະແກ້ໄຂຢ່າງຖືກຕ້ອງຕາມທີ່ຮ້ອງຂໍ. "
"ຖ້າທ່ານຄິດວ່າການປະຕິເສດຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານຂອງພວກເຮົາແມ່ນຜິດພາດດ້ວຍເຫດຜົນໃດກໍຕາມ, "
"ໃຫ້ພວກເຮົາຮູ້. ຜູ້ກວດສອບພະຍາຍາມເຮັດວຽກກັບທ່ານເພື່ອບັນລຸວິທີແກ້ໄຂທີ່ດີທີ່ສຸດສໍາລັບຜູ້ໃຊ້ຂອງພວກເຮົາ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:211
msgid "Merge and maintenance"
msgstr "ການລວມ (Merge) ແລະ ການບຳລຸງຮັກສາ"

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:213
msgid ""
"After ensuring your changeset meets all of our requirements, it becomes a "
"part of Ubuntu Touch. Thank you! You are a member of a small group of people "
"contributing to a beautiful community. However, this is not the end of the "
"work."
msgstr ""
"ຫຼັງຈາກໃຫ້ແນ່ໃຈວ່າຊຸດການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານກົງກັບຄວາມຕ້ອງການທັງໝົດຂອງພວກເຮົາ, "
"ມັນຈະກາຍເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງ Ubuntu Touch. ຂໍຂອບໃຈ! "
"ທ່ານເປັນສະມາຊິກຂອງກຸ່ມຄົນຂະໜາດນ້ອຍທີ່ປະກອບສ່ວນເຂົ້າໃນຊຸມຊົນທີ່ສວຍງາມ. ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, "
"ນີ້ບໍ່ແມ່ນຈຸດສິ້ນສຸດຂອງວຽກງານ."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:215
msgid ""
"Sometimes your changes break a piece of Ubuntu Touch functionality despite "
"our best efforts. You might be called upon to help investigate the source of "
"the issue and prepare a fix if this happens. Your change could be reverted "
"if we find that your change was the direct cause of a bug and we cannot "
"contact you."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານເຮັດໃຫ້ຟັງຊັນຂອງ Ubuntu Touch ເສຍຫາຍ "
"ເຖິງແມ່ນວ່າພວກເຮົາຈະພະຍາຍາມຢ່າງເຕັມທີ່ແລ້ວກໍຕາມ. "
"ທ່ານອາດຈະຖືກຮຽກຮ້ອງໃຫ້ຊ່ວຍສືບສວນແຫຼ່ງທີ່ມາຂອງບັນຫາ ແລະ ກະກຽມການແກ້ໄຂຖ້າສິ່ງນີ້ເກີດຂຶ້ນ. "
"ການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານອາດຈະຖືກຍົກເລີກ (reverted) "
"ຖ້າພວກເຮົາພົບວ່າການປ່ຽນແປງຂອງທ່ານແມ່ນສາເຫດໂດຍກົງຂອງບັກ ແລະ ພວກເຮົາບໍ່ສາມາດຕິດຕໍ່ທ່ານໄດ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:217
msgid ""
"New contributors might notice that you have recently worked on a component "
"they want to work with. We would be grateful if you helped teach them what "
"you learned during this process."
msgstr ""
"ຜູ້ປະກອບສ່ວນໃໝ່ອາດຈະສັງເກດເຫັນວ່າທ່ານໄດ້ເຮັດວຽກກັບອົງປະກອບທີ່ພວກເຂົາຕ້ອງການເຮັດວຽກນຳ. "
"ພວກເຮົາຈະຂອບໃຈຖ້າທ່ານຊ່ວຍສອນພວກເຂົາກ່ຽວກັບສິ່ງທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ຮຽນຮູ້ໃນລະຫວ່າງຂະບວນການນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/code.rst:219
msgid ""
"If nothing else, stick around for the people thanking you for the change "
"you've made. The Ubuntu Touch community is incredibly supportive and "
"thankful. It would be a shame for you to miss your share of the good vibes."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າງໜ້ອຍທີ່ສຸດ, ໃຫ້ຢູ່ລໍຖ້າຄົນທີ່ຂອບໃຈທ່ານສຳລັບການປ່ຽນແປງທີ່ທ່ານໄດ້ເຮັດ. ຊຸມຊົນ Ubuntu Touch "
"ແມ່ນສະຫນັບສະໜູນ ແລະ ຮູ້ບຸນຄຸນຢ່າງບໍ່ໜ້າເຊື່ອ. "
"ມັນຈະເປັນເລື່ອງໜ້າເສຍດາຍຖ້າທ່ານພາດສ່ວນແບ່ງຂອງຄວາມຮູ້ສຶກດີໆຂອງທ່ານ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:2
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "ເອກະສານ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:5
msgid ""
"Documentation on this site is written in ReStructuredText, or RST for short. "
"Please check the `RST Primer <http://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/stable/"
"rest.html>`_ if you are not familiar with RST."
msgstr ""
"ເອກະສານຢູ່ໃນເວັບໄຊທ໌ນີ້ຖືກຂຽນເປັນ ReStructuredText, ຫຼື RST ໂດຍຫຍໍ້. ກະລຸນາກວດເບິ່ງ `RST "
"Primer <http://www.sphinx-doc.org/en/stable/rest.html>`_ ຖ້າທ່ານບໍ່ຄຸ້ນເຄີຍກັບ RST."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:7
msgid ""
"This page will guide you through writing great documentation for the UBports "
"project that can be featured on this site."
msgstr ""
"ໜ້ານີ້ຈະແນະນຳທ່ານຜ່ານການຂຽນເອກະສານທີ່ດີສຳລັບໂຄງການ UBports ທີ່ສາມາດນຳສະເໜີຢູ່ໃນເວັບໄຊທ໌ນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:10
msgid "Documentation guidelines"
msgstr "ຄຳແນະນຳກ່ຽວກັບເອກະສານ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:12
msgid ""
"These rules govern how you should write documentation to avoid problems with "
"style, format or linking."
msgstr ""
"ກົດລະບຽບເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຄວບຄຸມວິທີທີ່ທ່ານຄວນຂຽນເອກະສານເພື່ອຫຼີກເວັ້ນບັນຫາກັບຮູບແບບ, ການຈັດຮູບແບບ ຫຼື "
"ການເຊື່ອມຕໍ່."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:15
msgid "Title"
msgstr "ຫົວຂໍ້"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:17
msgid ""
"All pages must have a document title that will be shown in the table of "
"contents (left sidebar) and at the top of the page."
msgstr "ທຸກໜ້າຕ້ອງມີຫົວຂໍ້ເອກະສານທີ່ຈະສະແດງຢູ່ໃນສາລະບານ (ແຖບດ້ານຊ້າຍ) ແລະ ຢູ່ເທິງສຸດຂອງໜ້າ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:19
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Titles should be \"sentence cased\" rather than \"Title Cased\". For "
"example::"
msgstr ""
"ຫົວຂໍ້ຄວນຈະເປັນ \"ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ແບບປະໂຫຍກ (sentence cased)\" ແທນທີ່ຈະເປັນ \"ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ແບບຫົວຂໍ້ "
"(Title Cased)\". ຕົວຢ່າງ::"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:28
msgid ""
"There isn't a single definition of title casing that everyone follows, but "
"sentence casing is easy. This helps keep capitalization in the table of "
"contents consistent."
msgstr ""
"ບໍ່ມີຄຳນິຍາມດຽວຂອງການໃຊ້ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ໃນຫົວຂໍ້ທີ່ທຸກຄົນປະຕິບັດຕາມ, ແຕ່ການໃຊ້ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ແບບປະໂຫຍກແມ່ນງ່າຍ. "
"ນີ້ຊ່ວຍຮັກສາການໃຊ້ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ໃນສາລະບານໃຫ້ສອດຄ່ອງກັນ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:30
msgid ""
"Page titles are underlined with equals signs. For example, the markup "
"for :doc:`./bugreporting` includes the following title:"
msgstr ""
"ຫົວຂໍ້ໜ້າຖືກຂີດກ້ອງດ້ວຍເຄື່ອງໝາຍເທົ່າກັບ. ຕົວຢ່າງ, markup ສຳລັບ :doc:`./bugreporting` "
"ລວມມີຫົວຂໍ້ຕໍ່ໄປນີ້:"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:37
msgid "Note that:"
msgstr "ສັງເກດວ່າ:"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:39
msgid "The title is sentence cased"
msgstr "ຫົວຂໍ້ເປັນຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ແບບປະໂຫຍກ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:40
msgid "The title is underlined with equals signs"
msgstr "ຫົວຂໍ້ຖືກຂີດກ້ອງດ້ວຍເຄື່ອງໝາຍເທົ່າກັບ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:41
msgid "The underline spans the title completely without going over"
msgstr "ເສັ້ນຂີດກ້ອງກວມເອົາຫົວຂໍ້ທັງໝົດໂດຍບໍ່ເກີນ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:43
msgid "Incorrect examples of titles include:"
msgstr "ຕົວຢ່າງຫົວຂໍ້ທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງລວມມີ:"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:45
msgid "Incorrect casing"
msgstr "ການໃຊ້ຕົວພິມໃຫຍ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:52
msgid "Underline too short"
msgstr "ເສັ້ນຂີດກ້ອງສັ້ນເກີນໄປ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:59
msgid "Underline too long"
msgstr "ເສັ້ນຂີດກ້ອງຍາວເກີນໄປ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:68
msgid "Headings"
msgstr "ຫົວຂໍ້ຍ່ອຍ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:70
msgid ""
"There are several levels of headings that you may place on a page. These "
"levels are shown here in order:"
msgstr "ມີຫົວຂໍ້ຍ່ອຍຫຼາຍລະດັບທີ່ທ່ານສາມາດວາງໄວ້ໃນໜ້າ. ລະດັບເຫຼົ່ານີ້ຖືກສະແດງຢູ່ທີ່ນີ້ຕາມລຳດັບ:"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:86
msgid ""
"Please refrain from using more than four levels. If you think you need more "
"levels, it is a good sign that the document should be split up into multiple "
"pages. Furthermore the web version of the documentation only shows four "
"levels in it's table of contents."
msgstr ""
"ກະລຸນາຫຼີກເວັ້ນການໃຊ້ຫຼາຍກວ່າສີ່ລະດັບ. ຖ້າທ່ານຄິດວ່າທ່ານຕ້ອງການລະດັບເພີ່ມເຕີມ, "
"ມັນເປັນສັນຍານທີ່ດີວ່າເອກະສານຄວນຖືກແບ່ງອອກເປັນຫຼາຍໜ້າ. ນອກຈາກນັ້ນ, "
"ສະບັບເວັບຂອງເອກະສານສະແດງພຽງແຕ່ສີ່ລະດັບໃນສາລະບານຂອງມັນ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:89
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr "ສາລະບານ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:91
msgid ""
"If you add a new page you also have to add it to the table of contents. You "
"can do this by adding the page to the ``index.rst`` file in the same "
"directory where you created it. For example, if you create a file called "
"\"newpage.rst\", you would add the line marked with a chevron (>) in the "
"nearest index:"
msgstr ""
"ຖ້າທ່ານເພີ່ມໜ້າໃໝ່, ທ່ານຕ້ອງເພີ່ມມັນເຂົ້າໃນສາລະບານເຊັ່ນກັນ. "
"ທ່ານສາມາດເຮັດສິ່ງນີ້ໄດ້ໂດຍການເພີ່ມໜ້າເຂົ້າໃນໄຟລ໌ ``index.rst`` "
"ໃນໄດເຣັກທໍຣີດຽວກັນກັບບ່ອນທີ່ທ່ານສ້າງມັນ. ຕົວຢ່າງ, ຖ້າທ່ານສ້າງໄຟລ໌ທີ່ມີຊື່ວ່າ \"newpage.rst\", "
"ທ່ານຈະເພີ່ມແຖວທີ່ໝາຍດ້ວຍເຄື່ອງໝາຍ (> ) ໃນ index ທີ່ໃກ້ທີ່ສຸດ:"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:103
msgid ""
"The order matters. If you would like your page to appear in a certain "
"position in the table of contents, place it there. In the previous example, "
"newpage would be added to the end of this table of contents."
msgstr ""
"ລຳດັບມີຄວາມສຳຄັນ. ຖ້າທ່ານຕ້ອງການໃຫ້ໜ້າຂອງທ່ານປະກົດຢູ່ໃນຕຳແໜ່ງສະເພາະໃນສາລະບານ, "
"ໃຫ້ວາງມັນໄວ້ບ່ອນນັ້ນ. ໃນຕົວຢ່າງກ່ອນໜ້ານີ້, newpage ຈະຖືກເພີ່ມເຂົ້າໃນຕອນທ້າຍຂອງສາລະບານນີ້."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:106
msgid "Moving pages"
msgstr "ການຍ້າຍໜ້າ"

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:108
msgid ""
"Sometimes it becomes necessary to move a page from one place in the "
"documentation to another. Generally this is to improve document flow: For "
"example, it makes more sense for the page to come after a page you've just "
"added in a different section."
msgstr ""
"ບາງຄັ້ງມັນຈຳເປັນຕ້ອງຍ້າຍໜ້າຈາກບ່ອນໜຶ່ງໃນເອກະສານໄປຫາບ່ອນອື່ນ. ໂດຍທົ່ວໄປແລ້ວ "
"ນີ້ແມ່ນເພື່ອປັບປຸງການໄຫຼຂອງເອກະສານ: ຕົວຢ່າງ, "
"ມັນສົມເຫດສົມຜົນກວ່າສຳລັບໜ້າທີ່ຈະມາຫຼັງຈາກໜ້າທີ່ທ່ານຫາກໍເພີ່ມໃນພາກສ່ວນອື່ນ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:110
msgid ""
"However, people link to our documentation from many sources that we do not "
"control. Blogs, websites, and other documentation sites can direct people "
"here using links that they may never update. It is a terrible experience to "
"follow a link from a different site and land on a 404 page, being forced to "
"search manually in our documentation."
msgstr ""
"ຢ່າງໃດກໍຕາມ, ຄົນເຊື່ອມຕໍ່ກັບເອກະສານຂອງພວກເຮົາຈາກຫຼາຍແຫຼ່ງທີ່ພວກເຮົາບໍ່ໄດ້ຄວບຄຸມ. ບລັອກ, ເວັບໄຊທ໌, "
"ແລະ ເວັບໄຊທ໌ເອກະສານອື່ນໆສາມາດນຳພາຄົນມາທີ່ນີ້ໂດຍໃຊ້ລິ້ງທີ່ພວກເຂົາອາດຈະບໍ່ເຄີຍອັບເດດ. "
"ມັນເປັນປະສົບການທີ່ຂີ້ຮ້າຍທີ່ຈະຕິດຕາມລິ້ງຈາກເວັບໄຊທ໌ອື່ນ ແລະ ໄປຮອດໜ້າ 404, "
"ໂດຍຖືກບັງຄັບໃຫ້ຄົ້ນຫາດ້ວຍຕົນເອງໃນເອກະສານຂອງພວກເຮົາ."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:114
msgid ""
"We use a tool called Rediraffe to avoid such a bad experience. Rediraffe "
"creates redirect pages, which can send a user from an old, invalid link to a "
"new, useful link. Please create a redirect link when changing a page's name "
"or moving a page within the documentation's directory structure. Redirect "
"links are created by placing the filename of the old document and the "
"filename of the new document, relative to the documentation's root, in the "
"`redirects.txt file <https://gitlab.com/ubports/docs/docs.ubports.com/-/blob/"
"master/redirects.txt>`_."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ເຄື່ອງມືທີ່ມີຊື່ວ່າ Rediraffe ເພື່ອຫຼີກເວັ້ນປະສົບການທີ່ບໍ່ດີດັ່ງກ່າວ. Rediraffe "
"ສ້າງໜ້າການປ່ຽນເສັ້ນທາງ, ເຊິ່ງສາມາດສົ່ງຜູ້ໃຊ້ຈາກລິ້ງເກົ່າທີ່ບໍ່ຖືກຕ້ອງໄປຫາລິ້ງໃໝ່ທີ່ເປັນປະໂຫຍດ. "
"ກະລຸນາສ້າງລິ້ງການປ່ຽນເສັ້ນທາງເມື່ອປ່ຽນຊື່ໜ້າ ຫຼື ຍ້າຍໜ້າພາຍໃນໂຄງສ້າງໄດເຣັກທໍຣີຂອງເອກະສານ. "
"ລິ້ງການປ່ຽນເສັ້ນທາງຖືກສ້າງຂຶ້ນໂດຍການວາງຊື່ໄຟລ໌ຂອງເອກະສານເກົ່າ ແລະ ຊື່ໄຟລ໌ຂອງເອກະສານໃໝ່, "
"ທຽບກັບຮາກຖານຂອງເອກະສານ, ໃນ `ໄຟລ໌ redirects.txt <https://gitlab.com/ubports/"
"docs/docs.ubports.com/-/blob/master/redirects.txt>`_."

#: ../../contribute/documentation.rst:116
msgid ""
"We use Rediraffe's ``checkdiff`` builder to ensure that pages are not "
"deleted from the documentation without a redirect in place. This builder is "
"run as part of the ``build.sh`` script in the repository and as part of our "
"automated build once you submit a Merge Request (MR)."
msgstr ""
"ພວກເຮົາໃຊ້ ``checkdiff`` builder ຂອງ Rediraffe "
"ເພື່ອຮັບປະກັນວ່າໜ້າຕ່າງໆຈະບໍ່ຖືກລຶບອອກຈາກເອກະສານໂດຍບໍ່ມີການປ່ຽນເສັ້ນທາງ. Builder "
"ນີ້ຖືກດຳເນີນການເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງສະຄິບ ``build.sh`` ໃນ repository ແລະ ເປັນສ່ວນໜຶ່ງຂອງການ "
"build ອັດຕະໂນມັດຂອງພວກເຮົາເມື່ອທ່ານສົ່ງຄຳຮ້ອງຂໍການລວມ (Merge Request/MR)."

